    perf(write): dictionary size limit checked in-loop, stats after decision

    Both dictionary writers now fall back to PLAIN as soon as the dictionary
    exceeds dictionary_size_limit, instead of hashing the whole column first.
    The dictionary only grows, so the fallback decision and output bytes are
    unchanged. Statistics are computed after the dictionary is kept, since
    fallbacks compute their own. getOrPut replaces get+put. The explicit
    cardinality threshold behaves as before; the default stays "no check"
    (D3 default was dropped: it changes output bytes for mixed5).

    Bench (make bench, zig-only, ReleaseFast, best of 2 per cell; HEAD vs this commit):
    - str_unique write: 299.85 ms -> 97.94 ms (3.06x)
    - mixed5 write: 674.97 ms -> 278.49 ms (2.42x)
    - str_dict write: 73.32 ms -> 73.52 ms (flat)
    - int64/f64/int64_nullable write: flat within noise
    - file_MB unchanged for all scenarios (str_unique 13.25, mixed5 20.40, str_dict 0.84, int64 7.63, int64_nullable 5.21)

    Tests: golden-bytes test for the dictionary writers (hashes captured on
    pre-change code) passes; library tests pass on Zig 0.16 and 0.17 (zig-only).

